desc(
	mode: "source"
	language: "general"
	title: "Avoid Ssh Insecure Ignore Host Key"
	title_zh: "Avoid Ssh Insecure Ignore Host Key"
	type: vuln
	level: middle
	rule_id: "source-insecure-api-avoid-ssh-insecure-ignore-host-key"
	risk: "Security"
	desc: <<<DESC
Migrated from Semgrep rule `avoid-ssh-insecure-ignore-host-key` (go/lang/security/audit/crypto/insecure_ssh.yaml).
Original message: Disabled host key verification detected. This allows man-in-the-middle attacks. Use the 'golang.org/x/crypto/ssh/knownhosts' package to do host key verification. See https://skarlso.github.io/2019/02/17/go-ssh-with-host-key-verification/ to learn more about the problem and how to fix it.
CWE: CWE-322: Key Exchange without Entity Authentication
References:
- https://skarlso.github.io/2019/02/17/go-ssh-with-host-key-verification/
- https://gist.github.com/Skarlso/34321a230cf0245018288686c9e70b2d
Note: source-mode regex approximation of a safe-literal Semgrep pattern.
DESC
	solution: <<<SOLUTION
Review this occurrence and replace it with a safer alternative.
SOLUTION
	alert_min: 1
	"file://pos.go": <<<POS
ssh.InsecureIgnoreHostKey()
POS
	"safefile://pos.go": <<<NEG
ssh.FixedHostKey
NEG
)

${*.go}.pattern_regex(/(?:ssh\.InsecureIgnoreHostKey\(\))/) as $hit
alert $hit for {
	level: "middle",
	title: "Avoid Ssh Insecure Ignore Host Key",
	title_zh: "Avoid Ssh Insecure Ignore Host Key",
	message: "Avoid Ssh Insecure Ignore Host Key detected.",
}
